Mark XXVIII: living presence (wake phrase + ambient + personality)

- Wake phrase: configurable (voice.wake_phrase, default "Hey UMBRA"),
  honored by jarvis wake end to end - status line, partial matching, and
  prefix stripping; the JARVIS aliases remain accepted as the
  in-experience alias. Push-to-talk fallback unchanged.
- Ambient nudges (ambient.py, pure + testable): low battery, due
  reminders, health-band shifts - one concise nudge per evaluation,
  per-signal rate limiting (default 5 min), quiet hours (windows may
  cross midnight), wired into the sentinel daemon. Strictly opt-in:
  config ambient.nudges defaults to False; per-signal toggles
  (battery/reminders/health). Nudges never fire during an active
  announcement and never repeat inside the window.
- Personality pack (personality.json - JSON over YAML is a deliberate
  stdlib choice, noted assumption): honorific, verbosity, humor,
  proactive. jarvis personality show/set with strict validation
  (verbosity enum, humor 0-10, proactive 0-2, honorific 1-24 chars);
  corrupt packs fall back to the default register. The honorific is
  applied to the sentinel's visible greetings; system-prompt plumbing
  is deferred (noted assumption - XXVIII acceptance is validation +
  defaults).
- Config: additive AmbientConfig section (schema stays v4) + wake_phrase
  on VoiceConfig; settings show/set cover all ambient keys.
- Tests: wake phrase + legacy alias; quiet-hours boundaries (midnight
  crossing, same-day window, bad bounds); rate limit; candidates from
  battery/reminders/health with per-signal gating; pick quiet/fired
  behavior; personality defaults/validation/persistence; ambient
  default OFF + config round-trip (incl. wake_phrase).
- Version 3.15.0.
